      "writtenOn": "2021-03-17T10:40:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Might be useful to still have a way to disable this\n\nCan we distinguish between bp2build_available not being set at all (in which case, convert)\n\nvs bp2build_available being explicitly set to false?\n\nE.g. I can imagine a scenario where we might want to convert 50 targets in some module, except for 1 or 2 bad targets. It would be annoying to have to opt in those good 50 targets. Easier to convert everything except 1 or 2 that were explicitly disabled\n\nIf you don\u0027t want to keep bp2build_available in the Blueprint files, maybe we could have a 3rd list, something like\n\nAllModules (ie subtree)\nvs\nModuleOptIn \nvs\nModuleOptOut (can overrule AllModules)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 131,
        "startChar": 47,
        "endLine": 131,
        "endChar": 72
      },
      "revId": "5f5f4ece824293455caf3262b30f1fed3623bd66",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8c52be31_a8da8931",
        "filename": "android/bazel.go",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 131,
      "author": {
        "id": 1687194
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-17T13:54:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed, something like this would be good.\n\nIn reading the design I was concerned that we may still have a couple modules in a package that are more difficult to convert. If we change `bp2build_available` to be a pointer to a bool should allow us to distinguish between not set and explicitly set to false.\n\nThis could also be a good way to think about the naming of the lists:\n\nBP2BUILD_DEFAULTS_TRUE_RECURSIVE\n\nBP2BUILD_DEFAULTS_FALSE",
      "parentUuid": "5ee9e0d0_f6ccc9d2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 131,
        "startChar": 47,
        "endLine": 131,
        "endChar": 72
      },
      "revId": "5f5f4ece824293455caf3262b30f1fed3623bd66",
